Another cheap implementation lever is the whitening step. Symmetric covariance whitening costs two dense matmuls plus an eigendecomposition; QR whitening gives exact sample covariance too, with a different orthogonal orientation and potentially lower FLOPs. I’m comparing that locally before touching `submission.py`.
